  {
   "id": "_QsiwfMHBgAJ",
   "from": "Crump, Ron",
   "author": "942ffec526d6a312",
   "date": "2016-06-30T12:09:50Z",
   "subject": "Re: how to remove the text of sample ids (e.g. Mock_0,Mock_1)  in MDS plot from a ggplot2 object",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "Hi,\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "\r<br>&gt;Could I edit their source code and regenerated a CummeRbund_v2 package\r<br>&gt;instead?\r<br>\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "If you want to do this kind of plot a lot, then I would suggest copying\r<br>the code for their MDSplot function and making your own copy, either with\r<br>the geom_text bit removed or with it&#39;s use parameterised.\r<br>\r<br>In the meantime, I had a quick play and this may help.\r<br>\r<br># Create a data.frame to play with:\r<br>DF &lt;- data.frame(x=1:10,y=1:10,l=letters[1:10],stringsAsFactors=FALSE)\r<br>\r<br># Create a simple ggplot object with text labelling:\r<br>zz&lt;-ggplot(DF)+geom_point(aes(x=x,y=y))+geom_text(aes(x=x,y=y,label=l),nudg\r<br>e_x=0.2)\r<br>\r<br>Then I took a look at zz:\r<br>\r<br>&gt; length(zz)\r<br>[1] 9\r<br>&gt; names(zz)\r<br>[1] &quot;data&quot;        &quot;layers&quot;      &quot;scales&quot;      &quot;mapping&quot;     &quot;theme&quot;\r<br>&quot;coordinates&quot;\r<br>[7] &quot;facet&quot;       &quot;plot_env&quot;    &quot;labels&quot;\r<br>&gt; zz$layers\r<br>[[1]]\r<br>mapping: x = x, y = y\r<br>geom_point: na.rm = FALSE\r<br>stat_identity: na.rm = FALSE\r<br>position_identity \r<br>\r<br>[[2]]\r<br>mapping: x = x, y = y, label = l\r<br>geom_text: parse = FALSE, check_overlap = FALSE, na.rm = FALSE\r<br>stat_identity: na.rm = FALSE\r<br>position_nudge\r<br>\r<br>\r<br>\r<br>\r<br>So zz$layers[2] appears to define the geom_text call (in my case, I guess\r<br>it may differ depending the order of creating layers in MDSplot).\r<br>\r<br>#Then I created a copy of zz\r<br>zz2&lt;-zz\r<br># and removed that layer\r<br>zz2$layers[2] &lt;- NULL\r<br>\r<br>And zz2 now has my plot without labelled points.\r<br>\r<br>\r<br>\r<br>I hope this is of some use in fixing up this plot. As you pointed out a\r<br>personalised MDSplot would be the better long term solution (but I\r<br>wouldn&#39;t go so far as creating a whole new cummeRbund_v2 package for it -\r<br>maybe you could maybe suggest additional options to control the plotting\r<br>to the package authors).\r<br>\r<br>Regards,\r<br>Ron.\r<br>\r<br>"
    ]
   ]
  }
 ]
